    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1440">

                <pb facs="1400" n="1390" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">026 China/7–2949</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of
                            State of a Conversation With President Truman
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-07-29">July 29, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chinese White Paper</hi>
                </p>
                <p>I left with the President the memorandum on the China White Paper,<anchor n="45"
                        xml:id="d1440-f1"/> first of all going through with him the various
                    questions to ask whether he wished to decide them now or later.</p>
                <p>The President decided the White Paper would be released and it should be released
                    as soon as possible. He will be given a copy to read over the weekend. He and I
                    thought tentatively that probably the very last part of next week would be the
                    best time. Statements by him and <pb facs="1401" n="1391" xml:id="pg1391"/> me
                    will be given to him on Monday, and he will tell us then the exact date, so that
                    we can go ahead with sending out copies, etc., etc.</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dean Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
